?rva00531720@Rva00531720@@QAEEII@Z	0x00531720	55	partial	Improvement on the bank: the /Ot flag (bank used /Os) gives 54B vs 53B and is the ONLY setting measured that puts idx in ESI as retail does. Flag sweep /Os /O1 /O2 /Ot /Ot+/Ob2 /Os+/Oy- with the bank body: /Os and /O1 are 53B with idx hoisted into ECX and the lea emitted before the branches; /Ot and /O2 are 54B with push esi + mov esi,[esp+0xc] and the lea inside each branch. /Ot matches retail for the first three instructions (mov edx,[esp+4] / mov eax,edx) and for the push esi / mov esi,[esp+0xc] pair; the remaining residue is two independent encoding choices. (1) retail tests b1 with d1 e8 (shr eax,1) as the FIRST shift and b2 with c1 ea 02 second, while /Ot schedules b2 first as c1 e8 02 then b1 as d1 ea -- mask scheduling, not declaration order, since reversing the && operands gave 59B with a saved-register frame. (2) retail emits ONE hoisted lea ecx,[ecx+esi*4+0xc] then test BYTE PTR [ecx+1],0x80 and test BYTE PTR [ecx+2],1 off ecx; /Ot emits the lea per branch and folds esi into the addressing mode (mov dl,BYTE PTR [ecx+esi*4+0xd]). Verified wrong and reverted: volatile on j forces an ebp frame (60B); unsigned int b1/b2 instead of unsigned char drops to 50B and loses the and-against-1 register form; Elem & reference instead of const unsigned char * gives the same 54B; inlining m_elems[idx] into both tests gives 51B with no ESI at all. t=20min model=space-bunny-alpha score=0.92 stash=reverse/attempts/0x00531720.cpp
?rva00496DA3@Rva00496DA3@@QAEPAXPAXABVAsciiString@@@Z	0x00496DA3	98	partial	Improvement on the bank: the bank was 94B missing the frame slot entirely (retail 98B). Making the loop counter volatile plus rewriting the for as a while with an explicit ++i produces the missing push ecx and reaches 99B -- the frame slot now exists and the empty-string tail starts at the right offset. The bank blamed "missing push ecx plus mov ebp-4 edi dead store"; the cause is that MSVC 7.1 at /O1 keeps a plain unsigned counter entirely in a register and never allocates a frame slot, and the only lever measured that forces the allocation is volatile on the counter. Remaining residue is one byte and one register choice: retail keeps the index in EDI AND stores it to [ebp-4] once before the loop (xor edi,edi then mov DWORD PTR [ebp-4],edi), so the increment stays register-resident and only the initial zero is spilled; volatile forces EVERY read and write of i to go through memory (add DWORD PTR [ebp-4],0x1 and cmp DWORD PTR [ebp-4],eax), which costs exactly the extra byte and re-reads the bound. Flag sweep at the bank flags is unchanged (/O1 99B, /O1+/GR- 99B, /O2 133B and wrong from the first byte). Verified wrong and reverted: __assume(&i != 0) is optimized away entirely and returns to 94B; an address-taken pointer local used to read the bound (unsigned *pi = &i with *pi in the condition) drops to 87B because the compiler forwards the register value and drops the store; a volatile unsigned *pi dereferenced for its side effect inside the loop gives 104B; a self-assignment i = i to force the pre-loop store gives 105B with a saved-register frame. t=20min model=space-bunny-alpha score=0.96 stash=reverse/attempts/0x00496da3.cpp
